<title>SOUTH AFRICA: S.African Sept trade surplus 666.7 million rand.</title>
<headline>S.African Sept trade surplus 666.7 million rand.</headline>
<dateline>PRETORIA 1996-10-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Africa recorded a trade surplus of 666.7 million rand in September from a 132.4 million rand surplus in August, latest South African Revenue Service figures show.</p>
<p>A Reuters consensus poll of economists forecast an average 720 million rand surplus.  </p>
<p>(Data in billions of rand - rounded)</p>
<p>			Sept '96	     Aug '96	   Sept '95</p>
<p>Exports		10.96		 10.68		9.35</p>
<p>Imports		10.29		 10.55		7.44</p>
<p>Balance		 0.67		  0.13		1.91</p>
<p>			Jan-Sept '96    Jan-Sept '95</p>
<p>Exports		89.30		 76.84</p>
<p>Imports		85.04		 73.62</p>
<p>Balance		 4.26		  3.22</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom (+27 11 482-1003)</p>
